{"parents": [], "prev": {"link": "../agent/", "title": "Agents"}, "next": {"link": "../plugins/", "title": "Plugins"}, "title": "Orchestrator", "meta": {}, "body": "<section id=\"orchestrator\">\n<h1>Orchestrator<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#orchestrator\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-orchestrator\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">RunMode</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">value</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">names</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">module</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">qualname</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">type</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">boundary</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/enum.html#enum.Enum\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Enum</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Execution mode for the Orchestrator main loop.</p>\n<p><strong>When to use STOP_ON_EMPTY:</strong>\n- Batch processing jobs with defined end\n- ETL pipelines\n- One-time data migrations\n- Testing scenarios</p>\n<p><strong>When to use DAEMON:</strong>\n- Web servers and APIs\n- Continuous monitoring systems\n- Event-driven architectures\n- Long-running services requiring CLI control</p>\n<p><strong>Important:</strong> DAEMON mode requires explicit shutdown via CLI\ncommand \u2018shutdown\u2019 or programmatic call to stop().</p>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode.STOP_ON_EMPTY\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">STOP_ON_EMPTY</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'stop_on_empty'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode.STOP_ON_EMPTY\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop when all agents finished</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode.DAEMON\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DAEMON</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'daemon'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode.DAEMON\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Keep running until explicitly shutdown</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorConfig</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">check_interval</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_workers</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_start_timeout</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_command_interface</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">command_zmq_address</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">allowed_commands</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">run_mode</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">history_max_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">history_payload_bytes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">BaseClassConfig</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Orchestrator configuration class.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>check_interval</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 The interval to check the agents. Defaults to 1.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_workers</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 The maximum number of workers that can run concurrently. Defaults to 5.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent_start_timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum time in seconds to wait for an agent to start. Defaults to 30.0.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>enable_command_interface</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>) \u2013 Enable external command interface via ZeroMQ over TCP. Defaults to True.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>command_zmq_address</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 ZeroMQ address for external commands. Defaults to \u201c<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"tcp://\">tcp://</a><a href=\"#id1\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id2\">*</span></a>:5555\u201d.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>logger</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.utilities.LoggerConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.utilities.LoggerConfig\"><em>LoggerConfig</em></a>) \u2013 Logger configuration.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>run_mode</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\"><em>RunMode</em></a>) \u2013 Required lifecycle policy. Defaults to RunMode.STOP_ON_EMPTY.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>history_max_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum number of events to store in history (ring buffer size). Defaults to 5000.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>history_payload_bytes</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum size for event payload data. Defaults to 256.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>check_interval</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_workers</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent_start_timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>enable_command_interface</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>bool</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>command_zmq_address</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>allowed_commands</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>set</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>run_mode</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\"><em>RunMode</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>history_max_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>history_payload_bytes</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.check_interval\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">check_interval</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">1</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.check_interval\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The interval to check the agents.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.max_workers\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">max_workers</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">5</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.max_workers\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The maximum number of workers that can run concurrently.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.agent_start_timeout\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_start_timeout</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">30.0</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.agent_start_timeout\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Maximum time in seconds to wait for an agent to start. Defaults to 30.0.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.enable_command_interface\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_command_interface</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">True</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.enable_command_interface\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Enable external command interface via ZeroMQ.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.command_zmq_address\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">command_zmq_address</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'tcp://*:5555'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.command_zmq_address\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>ZeroMQ address for external commands.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.allowed_commands\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">allowed_commands</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">set</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.allowed_commands\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Allowed commands for CLI interface. Can be a set of commands, a preset name, or None for all commands.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.run_mode\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">run_mode</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.RunMode\"><span class=\"pre\">RunMode</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">'stop_on_empty'</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.run_mode\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Execution mode for the orchestrator. Defaults to RunMode.STOP_ON_EMPTY.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.history_max_events\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">history_max_events</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">5000</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.history_max_events\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Maximum number of events to store in history (ring buffer size).</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.history_payload_bytes\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">history_payload_bytes</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">256</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.history_payload_bytes\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Maximum size for event payload data.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.validate\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">validate</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig.validate\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Override this method to implement custom validation logic in derived classes.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>List of validation results.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>List[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ValidationResult\">ValidationResult</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorPlugin</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">BaseClassPlugin</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Plugin class for the Orchestrator.</p>\n<p>This class can contain various plugins that extend orchestrator functionality.</p>\n<p>Plugins can be defined as class attributes (defaults) and overridden via constructor:</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>class MyOrchestratorPlugin(OrchestratorPlugin):</dt><dd><p>custom_plugin = CustomPlugin()</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p># Use default\nplugin1 = MyOrchestratorPlugin()</p>\n<p># Override heartbeat\nplugin2 = MyOrchestratorPlugin(heartbeat=OrchestratorHeartbeatPlugin())</p>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin.heartbeat\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">heartbeat</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../plugins/#PyOrchestrate.core.plugins.heartbeat.OrchestratorHeartbeatPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.plugins.heartbeat.OrchestratorHeartbeatPlugin\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorHeartbeatPlugin</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></em><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">None</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin.heartbeat\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Orchestrator</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">config</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">plugin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClass\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClass\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">BaseClass</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Orchestrator class to manages the agents.</p>\n<p>The Orchestrator provides centralized event management and coordination for all agents.\nAgents communicate with the orchestrator via message channels, and the orchestrator\nhandles all event processing and callback execution through its own event manager.</p>\n<p>This centralized approach eliminates event duplication and provides a single point\nof control for system-wide event handling.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>memory</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory\"><em>OMemory</em></a>) \u2013 Memory to store the agents.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_manager</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager\"><em>EventManager</em></a>) \u2013 Centralized event manager for handling all agent events.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>dependencies</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>list</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em><em>]</em>) \u2013 Dependencies among agents.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\"><em>OrchestratorConfig</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>plugin</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\"><em>OrchestratorPlugin</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.register_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">register_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.register_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Register an agent on the orchestrator.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><em>BaseClassConfig</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_plugin</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\"><em>BaseClassPlugin</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>ControlEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>StateEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>msg_channel</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\"><em>MessageChannel</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\"><em>AgentEntry</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.add_dependency\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_dependency</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.add_dependency\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add dependencies among agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>depends_on</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>list</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.validate_dependencies\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">validate_dependencies</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.validate_dependencies\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check for dependency errors.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.start\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.start\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start all registered agents.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.stop\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.stop\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop all registered agents.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.join\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">join</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.join\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Wait for all agents to complete.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.simple_join\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">simple_join</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.simple_join\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Simple join method to wait for all processes or threads to complete their execution.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.report\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">report</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.report\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Report the status of all agents.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.Config\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Config</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.Config\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>alias of <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorConfig</span></code></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.Plugin\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Plugin</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.Plugin\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>alias of <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorPlugin</span></code></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.config\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">config</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorConfig\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorConfig</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.config\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.plugin\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">plugin</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.OrchestratorPlugin\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorPlugin</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.plugin\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd></dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id0\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">register_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_class</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_config</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_plugin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">control_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">state_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">msg_channel</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id0\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Register an agent on the orchestrator.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<p>After registering the agent, you can call the <cite>start</cite> method to start all agents.</p>\n<p>Events from agents are handled centrally by the orchestrator\u2019s event manager.\nAgents communicate with the orchestrator via message channel.</p>\n<p>Delegates to AgentLifecycleManager.</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Warning</p>\n<p>agent_name must be unique.</p>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_class</strong> \u2013 Class of the agent to register.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><em>BaseClassConfig</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Custom configuration for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_plugin</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\"><em>BaseClassPlugin</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Custom plugin for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>ControlEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Control events for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>StateEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 State events for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>msg_channel</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\"><em>MessageChannel</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Message channel for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>kwargs</strong> \u2013 Additional arguments for the agent.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The agent entry object stored in the memory.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a></p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If an agent with the same name is already registered.</p></li>\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#Exception\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>Exception</strong></a> \u2013 If agent registration fails for any reason.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.register_event\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">register_event</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_type</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">callback</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.orchestrator.Orchestrator.register_event\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Register a callback function for a specific event type.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event_type</strong> \u2013 The type of event to listen for (e.g., OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_STARTED).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>callback</strong> \u2013 The callback function to execute when the event occurs.\nThe callback will receive the event data as arguments.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p>orchestrator.register_event(OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_STARTED, on_agent_start)\norchestrator.register_event(OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_TERMINATED, on_agent_terminated)</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id3\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_dependency</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">depends_on</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id3\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add dependencies: agent_name depends on depends_on.</p>\n<p>Validation is performed during validate_dependencies() call.\nDelegates entirely to DependencyGraph.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent that has dependencies</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>depends_on</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>list</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 List of agent names that agent_name depends on</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id4\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">validate_dependencies</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id4\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Validate dependency graph for errors (cycles, missing agents).</p>\n<p>Delegates entirely to DependencyGraph.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If validation fails (cycles or unregistered agents)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id5\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id5\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start all registered agents in the topological order of their dependencies.</p>\n<p>Delegates to WorkerPoolScheduler for agent startup.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id6\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id6\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Terminates all registered agents.</p>\n<p>Delegates to AgentLifecycleManager.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id7\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">join</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id7\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check the status of all agents and wait for them to complete.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<p>This method blocks the current thread until all agents are terminated.</p>\n<p>If command interface is enabled, the orchestrator will continue running\neven after all agents have finished, allowing remote control via CLI.\nUse the \u2018shutdown\u2019 command to terminate the orchestrator in this mode.</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>When agent is terminated, it emits an <cite>OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_TERMINATED</cite> event.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Uses WorkerPoolScheduler to manage agent termination and queue.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id8\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">simple_join</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id8\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Simple join method to wait for all processes or threads to complete their execution.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id9\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">report</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id9\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Report the status of all agents.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-lifecycle-manager\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Agent lifecycle management for registration, startup, and termination.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AgentLifecycleManager</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">memory</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">config</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">logger</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Manages the complete lifecycle of agents.</p>\n<p>This class handles:\n- Agent registration with validation\n- Agent startup with timeout protection\n- Agent termination (individual and bulk)\n- Configuration injection and validation</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">manager</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">AgentLifecycleManager</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">memory</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">config</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">logger</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">register_agent</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MyAgent</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent1&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">custom_config</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">config</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">success</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start_agent</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent1&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">stop_agent</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent1&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>memory</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory\"><em>OMemory</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><em>BaseClassConfig</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.register_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">register_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_class</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_config</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_plugin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">control_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">state_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">msg_channel</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.register_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Register an agent with the orchestrator.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_class</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#type\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>type</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\"><em>AgentProtocol</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 The agent class to instantiate</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Unique name for the agent</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><em>BaseClassConfig</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional custom configuration</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_plugin</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\"><em>BaseClassPlugin</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional custom plugin</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>ControlEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Control events for the agent</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>StateEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 State events for the agent</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>msg_channel</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\"><em>MessageChannel</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Message channel for agent communication</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>**kwargs</strong> \u2013 Additional arguments passed to agent</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The registered agent entry</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a></p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If agent name is not unique</p></li>\n<li><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ConfigValidationError\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.validation.ConfigValidationError\"><strong>ConfigValidationError</strong></a> \u2013 If agent config is invalid</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.start_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.start_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start an agent with timeout protection.</p>\n<p>Waits for agent.state_events.start_event with configured timeout.\nIf timeout is exceeded, attempts to stop the agent and returns False.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent to start</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>True if agent started successfully, False if timeout occurred</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If agent not found</p></li>\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#Exception\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>Exception</strong></a> \u2013 If agent.start() fails critically</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.stop_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.stop_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop a specific agent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent to stop</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If agent not found</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.stop_all\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop_all</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.stop_all\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop all registered agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.get_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.get_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Retrieve an agent entry by name.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The agent entry</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a></p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If agent not found</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.get_all_agents\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_all_agents</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager.get_all_agents\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get all registered agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>List of all agent entries</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">list</a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-dependency-graph\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Dependency graph management for agent dependencies.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DependencyGraph</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Manages dependency relationships between agents.</p>\n<p>This class handles the dependency graph for agents, providing methods to:\n- Add dependencies between agents\n- Validate the graph for correctness (no cycles, valid nodes)\n- Compute topological sort order for agent startup</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">DependencyGraph</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">add_dependency</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent_a&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent_b&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">validate</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent_a&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent_b&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">order</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">topological_sort</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent_a&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent_b&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">order</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># [&#39;agent_b&#39;, &#39;agent_a&#39;]</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.add_dependency\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_dependency</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">depends_on</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.add_dependency\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add dependency: agent_name depends on depends_on agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the dependent agent</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>depends_on</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>list</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 List of agent names that must start before agent_name</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.validate\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">validate</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">valid_agent_names</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.validate\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Validate the dependency graph.</p>\n<p>Checks:\n1. All referenced agent names exist in valid_agent_names\n2. No circular dependencies exist</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>valid_agent_names</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>set</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 Set of all registered agent names</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If validation fails (missing agents or cycles detected)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.topological_sort\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">topological_sort</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_names</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.topological_sort\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compute topological ordering of agents respecting dependencies.</p>\n<p>Uses Kahn\u2019s algorithm (BFS) to compute the ordering.\nAgents with no dependencies come first, followed by their dependents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_names</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>set</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 Set of all agent names to order</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Agents in topological order (dependencies before dependents)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">list</a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If graph has not been validated or contains cycles</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.get_dependencies\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_dependencies</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.get_dependencies\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get list of dependencies for a specific agent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>List of agent names this agent depends on</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">list</a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.has_dependencies\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">has_dependencies</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.dependency_graph.DependencyGraph.has_dependencies\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if any dependencies are defined.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if at least one dependency exists, False otherwise</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-worker-pool\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Worker pool and agent scheduling queue management.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">WorkerPoolScheduler</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_workers</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">lifecycle_manager</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">logger</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Manages worker pool and agent scheduling queue.</p>\n<p>This class handles:\n- Enforcing max_workers limit\n- Queueing agents when limit is reached\n- Automatically scheduling agents from queue when slots free up\n- Tracking running agent count</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">scheduler</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">WorkerPoolScheduler</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">max_workers</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">lifecycle_manager</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">logger</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">scheduler</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start_agent</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent1&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># Starts immediately if slot available</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">scheduler</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start_agent</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent2&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># Queued if at capacity</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">scheduler</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">on_agent_terminated</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent1&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># Starts next queued agent</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>max_workers</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>lifecycle_manager</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.lifecycle_manager.AgentLifecycleManager\"><em>AgentLifecycleManager</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.can_start_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">can_start_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.can_start_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if there\u2019s capacity to start a new agent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if running_agents &lt; max_workers, False otherwise</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.start_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.start_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start an agent immediately or queue it if at capacity.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent to start</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>True if agent started, False if queued</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.on_agent_terminated\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">on_agent_terminated</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.on_agent_terminated\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Callback when an agent terminates.</p>\n<p>Decrements running count and starts next queued agent if available.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the terminated agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.all_finished\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">all_finished</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.all_finished\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if all agents have finished (none running, none queued).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if no agents running and queue is empty</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.queue_size\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">queue_size</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.queue_size\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get current size of the waiting queue.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Number of agents waiting in queue</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.running_count\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">running_count</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.running_count\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get number of currently running agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Number of agents currently running</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.get_stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.worker_pool.WorkerPoolScheduler.get_stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get current scheduler statistics.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Statistics including running count, queue size, capacity</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">dict</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-event-bus\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Orchestrator Event Bus.</p>\n<p>This module provides the OrchestratorEventBus class that wraps EventManager and EventStore\nto provide a unified interface for event emission and history tracking. It automatically\nrecords events to the event store when they are emitted, simplifying event management.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrchestratorEventBus</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_store</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Centralized event system with automatic history tracking.</p>\n<p>The OrchestratorEventBus combines EventManager (for callbacks) and EventStore\n(for history) into a single, unified interface. When events are emitted, they\nare automatically tracked to the event store, eliminating the need for manual\nhistory recording.</p>\n<p>This class provides:\n- Event callback registration via EventManager\n- Automatic event history tracking to EventStore\n- Query API for event history analysis\n- Unified interface for all event operations</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id10\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id11\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id12\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id13\">`</span></a>python\nevent_store = EventStore(capacity=1000)\nevent_bus = OrchestratorEventBus(event_store)</p>\n<p># Register callback\nevent_bus.register_callback(</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_STARTED,\nlambda agent_name: print(f\u201dAgent {agent_name} started\u201d)</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<p>)</p>\n<p># Emit event (automatically tracked to history)\nevent_bus.emit(OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_STARTED, agent_name=\u201dagent1\u201d)</p>\n<p># Query history\nhistory = event_bus.get_history(agent_name=\u201dagent1\u201d)\n<a href=\"#id14\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id15\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id16\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id17\">`</span></a></p>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Thread Safety:</dt><dd><p>Both EventManager and EventStore are thread-safe, making this class\nsafe for use in multi-threaded environments.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>event_store</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore\"><em>EventStore</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.register_callback\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">register_callback</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_type</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">callback</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.register_callback\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Register a callback for a specific event type.</p>\n<p>The callback will be invoked whenever the event is emitted. Callbacks\nreceive event data as keyword arguments.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event_type</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\"><em>OrchestratorEvent</em></a>) \u2013 The orchestrator event to listen for</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>callback</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Callable\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Callable</em></a>) \u2013 Function to call when event occurs (receives event data as kwargs)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id18\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id19\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id20\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id21\">`</span></a>python\ndef on_agent_ready(agent_name: str, <a href=\"#id22\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id23\">**</span></a>kwargs):</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>print(f\u201dAgent {agent_name} is ready\u201d)</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>event_bus.register_callback(</dt><dd><p>OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_READY,\non_agent_ready</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<section id=\"id24\">\n<h3>)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id24\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>\n</section>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.emit\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">emit</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_type</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.emit\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Emit an event and automatically track it to history.</p>\n<p>This method performs two operations:\n1. Emits the event to all registered callbacks via EventManager\n2. Records the event to EventStore for history tracking</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event_type</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event.OrchestratorEvent\"><em>OrchestratorEvent</em></a>) \u2013 The orchestrator event to emit</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>**kwargs</strong> \u2013 Event data passed to callbacks and stored in history</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id25\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id26\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id27\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id28\">`</span></a>python\nevent_bus.emit(</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>OrchestratorEvent.AGENT_ERROR,\nagent_name=\u201dagent1\u201d,\nerror_message=\u201dConnection failed\u201d</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<section id=\"id29\">\n<h3>)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id29\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>\n</section>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.get_history\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_history</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_type</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">limit</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.get_history\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Query event history.</p>\n<p>Returns a list of event records matching the specified filters.\nIf no filters are provided, returns all events.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by agent name (optional)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_type</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by event type (optional)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>limit</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum number of events to return (default: 100)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>List of matching event records</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>List[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\">EventRecord</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id30\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id31\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id32\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id33\">`</span></a>python\n# Get all events for specific agent\nagent_events = event_bus.get_history(agent_name=\u201dagent1\u201d)</p>\n<p># Get last 10 error events\nerrors = event_bus.get_history(</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>event_type=\u201dagent_error\u201d,\nlimit=10</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<section id=\"id34\">\n<h3>)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id34\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>\n</section>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.get_agent_timeline\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent_timeline</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">limit</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.get_agent_timeline\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get complete event timeline for a specific agent.</p>\n<p>Returns all events related to the specified agent in chronological order.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>limit</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum number of events to return (default: 100)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Chronological list of events for the agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>List[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\">EventRecord</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id35\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id36\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id37\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id38\">`</span></a>python\ntimeline = event_bus.get_agent_timeline(\u201cagent1\u201d)\nfor event in timeline:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>print(f\u201d{event.timestamp}: {event.event_name}\u201d)</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"#id39\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id40\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id41\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id42\">`</span></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.get_stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.get_stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get event statistics.</p>\n<p>Returns statistics about recorded events, optionally filtered by agent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Agent name to filter statistics (optional)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Statistics dictionary with event counts</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">dict</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id43\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id44\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id45\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id46\">`</span></a>python\n# Global statistics\nglobal_stats = event_bus.get_stats()</p>\n<p># Agent-specific statistics\nagent_stats = event_bus.get_stats(agent_name=\u201dagent1\u201d)\n<a href=\"#id47\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id48\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id49\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id50\">`</span></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.shutdown\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">shutdown</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_bus.OrchestratorEventBus.shutdown\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Shutdown the event bus.</p>\n<p>Stops the EventManager\u2019s executor and prevents new event emissions.\nCall this method during orchestrator shutdown to ensure clean termination.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">`python</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">#</span> <span class=\"pre\">During</span> <span class=\"pre\">orchestrator</span> <span class=\"pre\">shutdown</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">event_bus.shutdown()</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">`</span></code></p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-event-store\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Event Store for PyOrchestrate - Ring buffer based event history</p>\n<p>This module provides efficient, lock-safe event storage with constant memory usage.\nUses a ring buffer (deque with maxlen) for O(1) append operations and minimal overhead.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EventRecord</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">seq</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">t_wall</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">t_mono_ns</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">category</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">severity</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.NamedTuple\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">NamedTuple</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Immutable event record with minimal overhead.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>seq</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Sequential event number</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>t_wall</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Wall clock time (time.time())</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>t_mono_ns</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Monotonic time in nanoseconds for robust ordering</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>category</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event category (\u201corchestrator\u201d | \u201cagent\u201d | \u201ccli\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event type (e.g., \u201cAGENT_STARTED\u201d, \u201cQUEUED\u201d, \u201cCLI_COMMAND\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Agent name if applicable</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>severity</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event severity (\u201cINFO\u201d | \u201cWARN\u201d | \u201cERROR\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>data</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional payload data (truncated for efficiency)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>seq</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>t_wall</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>t_mono_ns</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>category</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>severity</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>data</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.seq\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">seq</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.seq\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 0</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.t_wall\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">t_wall</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.t_wall\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 1</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.t_mono_ns\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">t_mono_ns</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.t_mono_ns\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 2</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.category\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">category</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.category\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 3</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.event_name\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.event_name\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 4</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 5</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.severity\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">severity</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.severity\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 6</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py attribute\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.data\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">dict</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.data\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Alias for field number 7</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.to_dict\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.to_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return a JSON-serializable dict representation of the event.</p>\n<p>Includes an ISO8601 <cite>timestamp</cite> string for convenience while preserving\nnumeric <cite>t_wall</cite> and <cite>t_mono_ns</cite> for consumers that need them.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">object</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.to_json\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_json</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">json_kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord.to_json\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return a JSON string representation of the event.</p>\n<p>Passes json_kwargs to json.dumps (e.g. indent=2, ensure_ascii=False).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">StorePolicy</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">args</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Protocol\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Protocol</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Protocol that defines the interface for event storage policies.</p>\n<p>Implementations can optimize storage strategies based on specific event types\n(e.g., keep only latest heartbeat per agent vs. full history for errors).</p>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.append\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">append</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">e</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.append\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add a new event record to the store.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>e</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.last\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">last</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">after_seq</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.last\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Retrieve the last N events with optional filtering.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>n</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>after_seq</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get event count statistics, optionally for a specific agent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.capacity_info\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">capacity_info</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy.capacity_info\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get capacity and usage information for this store.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">RingBufferStore</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">capacity</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">StorePolicy</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Fixed-capacity ring buffer store for event history.</p>\n<p>Features:\n- FIFO behavior: oldest events are automatically evicted when capacity is reached\n- O(1) append operations with constant memory usage\n- Maintains real-time event count statistics\n- Suitable for general event storage (errors, status changes, etc.)</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>capacity</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.append\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">append</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">e</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.append\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add a new event to the ring buffer.</p>\n<p>If the buffer is at capacity, the oldest event is automatically removed.\nUpdates internal statistics counters for fast stats() queries.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>e</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>) \u2013 Event record to store</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.last\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">last</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">after_seq</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.last\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Retrieve the most recent events from the ring buffer.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>n</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum number of events to return</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by specific agent name</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by specific event type</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>after_seq</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Only return events with sequence number &gt; after_seq</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>List of EventRecord objects, most recent last</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get event count statistics with O(1) complexity.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 If provided, return stats only for this agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Dictionary with event_name -&gt; count mappings</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.capacity_info\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">capacity_info</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.RingBufferStore.capacity_info\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get current capacity and usage information for the ring buffer.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Dictionary with capacity, current_size, oldest_seq, newest_seq</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">BucketRingStore</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">per_agent_capacity</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">StorePolicy</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Per-agent ring buffer store optimized for tracking latest events per agent.</p>\n<p>Features:\n- Separate ring buffer for each agent (bounded per-agent history)\n- Perfect for heartbeat monitoring: keeps only last N heartbeats per agent\n- O(1) append, efficient agent-specific queries\n- Events without agent are stored in a shared \u201c_none\u201d bucket\n- Memory usage scales with number of active agents</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>per_agent_capacity</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.append\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">append</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">e</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.append\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add event to the appropriate agent bucket.</p>\n<p>Creates new buckets automatically for new agents.\nOldest events are evicted when per-agent capacity is reached.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>e</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>) \u2013 Event record to store</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.last\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">last</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">after_seq</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.last\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Retrieve recent events from per-agent buckets.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>n</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum number of events to return</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 If specified, only return events from this agent\u2019s bucket</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by specific event type</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>after_seq</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Only return events with sequence number &gt; after_seq</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>List of EventRecord objects, sorted by sequence number (most recent last)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get event count statistics.</p>\n<p>Note: Currently not implemented for BucketRingStore.\nUse capacity_info() for basic usage statistics instead.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Agent to get stats for (ignored)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#NotImplementedError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>NotImplementedError</strong></a> \u2013 Always raised</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.capacity_info\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">capacity_info</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.BucketRingStore.capacity_info\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get capacity and usage information for all agent buckets.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Dictionary with per_agent_capacity, agents_known, approx_total_capacity,\ncurrent_size, oldest_seq, newest_seq</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EventStore</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">capacity</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">5000</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">payload_max_bytes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">256</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_policies</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>High-performance event storage with constant memory usage.</p>\n<p>Features:\n- Ring buffer with fixed capacity (no memory growth)\n- Thread-safe operations with minimal locking\n- Truncated payload to prevent memory bloat\n- Real-time aggregated counters for instant reports\n- Robust temporal ordering with monotonic timestamps\n- Pluggable storage policies per category (e.g., ring buffer vs. per-agent last-N)</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>capacity</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>payload_max_bytes</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_policies</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.StorePolicy\"><em>StorePolicy</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.record\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">record</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">category</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">severity</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'INFO'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.record\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Record a new event with O(1) complexity.</p>\n<p>Events are routed to appropriate storage policies based on event_name.\nIf no specific policy exists for the event_name, uses the default ring buffer.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>category</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event category (\u201corchestrator\u201d, \u201cagent\u201d, \u201ccli\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event type (e.g., \u201cagent_heartbeat\u201d, \u201cagent_error\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Agent name (optional, for agent-specific events)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>severity</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event severity level (\u201cINFO\u201d, \u201cWARN\u201d, \u201cERROR\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>data</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>dict</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Optional payload data (will be truncated if too long)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id51\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id52\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id53\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id54\">`</span></a>python\nstore.record(</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>category=\u201dagent\u201d,\nevent_name=\u201dagent_heartbeat\u201d,\nagent=\u201dworker1\u201d,\ndata={\u201ctimestamp\u201d: \u201c2023-08-19T10:30:00\u201d}</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<section id=\"id55\">\n<h3>)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id55\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>\n</section>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.last\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">last</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">after_seq</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.last\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Retrieve recent events with optional filtering.</p>\n<p>Storage behavior:\n- If event_name is None: Merges results from all configured stores (default + any event-specific stores)\n- If event_name is specified: Uses the event-specific store if configured,</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>otherwise falls back to the default ring buffer</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<p>This design allows optimized storage per event type while maintaining\nbackward compatibility for general queries.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>n</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum number of events to return</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by agent name (only events from this agent)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Filter by event type (single event name only).\nIf None, searches in the default store containing all events.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>after_seq</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>int</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Return only events after this sequence number</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>List of EventRecord objects, ordered by sequence number (most recent last)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Examples</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id56\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id57\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id58\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id59\">`</span></a>python\n# Get last 50 events of any type (uses default ring buffer)\nall_events = store.last(50)</p>\n<p># Get last 10 heartbeats (uses heartbeat-specific store if configured)\nheartbeats = store.last(10, event_name=\u201dagent_heartbeat\u201d)</p>\n<p># Get last 20 events from specific agent (any event type)\nagent_events = store.last(20, agent=\u201dworker1\u201d)</p>\n<p># Get heartbeats from specific agent\nagent_heartbeats = store.last(5, agent=\u201dworker1\u201d, event_name=\u201dagent_heartbeat\u201d)\n<a href=\"#id60\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id61\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id62\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id63\">`</span></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.latest\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">latest</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.latest\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the latest event of a specific type, optimized for O(1) access.</p>\n<p>Perfect for heartbeat monitoring and status checks.\nUses the event-specific store if configured, providing efficient access\nto the most recent event without scanning through history.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event type to look for (e.g., \u201cagent_heartbeat\u201d)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Agent name. If None, gets latest across all agents</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Latest EventRecord or None if not found</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id64\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id65\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id66\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id67\">`</span></a>python\n# Check if agent is alive (latest heartbeat)\nlatest_hb = store.latest(\u201cagent_heartbeat\u201d, \u201cworker1\u201d)\nif latest_hb and time.time() - latest_hb.t_wall &lt; 30:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>print(\u201cAgent is alive\u201d)</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"#id68\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id69\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id70\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id71\">`</span></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.latest_all_agents\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">latest_all_agents</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.latest_all_agents\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the latest event of a specific type for all agents.</p>\n<p>Extremely useful for heartbeat monitoring: get the last heartbeat\nfrom every agent in a single O(agents) operation.</p>\n<p>Optimized implementations:\n- BucketRingStore: Iterates through per-agent buckets efficiently\n- RingBufferStore: Scans events and groups by agent</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>event_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Event type to look for (e.g., \u201cagent_heartbeat\u201d)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Dictionary mapping agent_name -&gt; latest EventRecord\n(excludes agents with no events of this type)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventRecord\"><em>EventRecord</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id72\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id73\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id74\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id75\">`</span></a>python\n# Monitor all agent heartbeats\nheartbeats = store.latest_all_agents(\u201cagent_heartbeat\u201d)\nfor agent, hb in heartbeats.items():</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>age = time.time() - hb.t_wall\nif age &gt; 30:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>print(f\u201dAgent {agent} missed heartbeat ({age:.1f}s ago)\u201d)</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n</div></blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"#id76\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id77\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id78\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id79\">`</span></a></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get aggregated event count statistics with O(1) complexity.</p>\n<p>Note: Currently only provides statistics from the default ring buffer store.\nEvent-specific stores may not implement stats collection.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>) \u2013 Get stats for specific agent, or global stats if None</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Dictionary with \u201cby_type\u201d key containing event_name -&gt; count mappings</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Dict</em></a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">int</a>]]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">`python</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">stats</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">store.stats()</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">print(f&quot;Total</span> <span class=\"pre\">heartbeats:</span> <span class=\"pre\">{stats['by_type'].get('agent_heartbeat',</span> <span class=\"pre\">0)}&quot;)</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">`</span></code></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.get_capacity_info\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_capacity_info</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore.get_capacity_info\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get current capacity and usage information for all storage policies.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>\u201cstores\u201d: Dictionary mapping store_name -&gt; capacity_info for ALL stores\n- \u201c__default__\u201d: The default RingBufferStore capacity info\n- event-specific stores (e.g., \u201cagent_heartbeat\u201d): Custom store capacity info</p></li>\n<li><p>\u201dsummary\u201d: High-level aggregated information\n- \u201ctotal_stores\u201d: Total number of configured stores\n- \u201ctotal_events\u201d: Approximate total events across all stores</p></li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Dictionary with</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p>Useful for monitoring memory usage and detecting storage issues.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">`python</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">info</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">store.get_capacity_info()</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">default_info</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">info['stores']['__default__']</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">hb_info</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">info['stores'].get('agent_heartbeat',</span> <span class=\"pre\">{})</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">total_stores</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">info['summary']['total_stores']</span>\n<span class=\"pre\">`</span></code></p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-message-router\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Message Router for Orchestrator.</p>\n<p>This module provides the MessageRouter class that handles routing of agent messages\nto the orchestrator event system. It includes thread-safe tracking of terminated agents\nto filter stale messages (e.g., heartbeats from agents that have already terminated).</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">MessageRouter</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_manager</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message_channel</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">logger</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Routes messages from agents to orchestrator event system.</p>\n<p>The MessageRouter is responsible for:\n- Converting agent STATUS messages to orchestrator events\n- Filtering stale heartbeat messages from terminated agents\n- Thread-safe tracking of agent termination states\n- Emitting events to registered callbacks via EventManager</p>\n<p>This class isolates message routing logic from the main Orchestrator,\nmaking it easier to test and maintain.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id80\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id81\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id82\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id83\">`</span></a>python\nevent_manager = EventManager()\nrouter = MessageRouter(event_manager, logger)</p>\n<p># Process incoming agent message\nrouter.route_agent_message(service_message)</p>\n<p># Mark agent as terminated\nrouter.mark_agent_terminated(\u201cagent_name\u201d)\n<a href=\"#id84\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id85\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id86\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id87\">`</span></a></p>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Thread Safety:</dt><dd><p>All methods that access <cite>_terminated_agents</cite> are thread-safe and can be\ncalled from multiple threads concurrently.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>event_manager</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.event_manager.EventManager\"><em>EventManager</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>message_channel</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\"><em>MessageChannel</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>logger</strong> (<em>Logger</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.start\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.start\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start the message router and its channel handler.</p>\n<p>Creates and starts a ChannelHandler to process incoming agent messages.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.stop\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">timeout</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">2.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.stop\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop the message router and its channel handler.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum time to wait for handler thread to stop</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.is_running\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_running</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.is_running\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if the message router is currently running.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if running, False otherwise</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.route_agent_message\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">route_agent_message</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">msg</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.route_agent_message\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Process and route a message from an agent.</p>\n<p>Converts agent STATUS messages to orchestrator events.\nFilters stale heartbeat messages from terminated agents.</p>\n<p>Only STATUS messages are processed. Other message types are ignored\nwith a warning log entry.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>msg</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a>) \u2013 The service message from an agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>AGENT_CLOSE: Marks agent as terminated and emits AGENT_TERMINATED event</p></li>\n<li><p>AGENT_START: Emits AGENT_STARTED event</p></li>\n<li><p>AGENT_READY: Emits AGENT_READY event</p></li>\n<li><p>AGENT_HEARTBEAT: Emits AGENT_HEARTBEAT event (filtered if agent terminated)</p></li>\n<li><p>ERROR: Emits AGENT_ERROR event with error message</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.mark_agent_terminated\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">mark_agent_terminated</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.mark_agent_terminated\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Mark an agent as terminated to filter future stale messages.</p>\n<p>This is a thread-safe operation that updates the internal set of\nterminated agents. Once marked, heartbeat messages from this agent\nwill be filtered out.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the terminated agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.is_agent_terminated\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_agent_terminated</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.is_agent_terminated\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if an agent has been marked as terminated.</p>\n<p>This is a thread-safe operation that checks the internal set of\nterminated agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent to check</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>True if agent is terminated, False otherwise</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.reset_termination_state\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">reset_termination_state</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.reset_termination_state\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Reset termination state for an agent.</p>\n<p>This is useful for scenarios where an agent might be restarted\nand should no longer be considered terminated.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Name of the agent</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.get_terminated_agents\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_terminated_agents</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.message_router.MessageRouter.get_terminated_agents\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get a copy of the set of terminated agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Copy of terminated agents set (thread-safe)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Set[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-command-interface\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Command Interface for Orchestrator.</p>\n<p>This module provides the CommandInterface class that manages external command\nprocessing for the orchestrator. It encapsulates ZeroMQ command channel setup,\ncommand handler integration, and message processing logic.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CommandInterface</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">orchestrator</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">zmq_address</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">allowed_commands</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">event_store</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">logger</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Manages external command interface for orchestrator.</p>\n<p>The CommandInterface encapsulates all logic for handling external commands\nfrom CLI clients. It manages:\n- ZeroMQ ROUTER socket for command communication\n- CommandHandler for executing commands\n- ChannelHandler for async message processing\n- Event tracking for command execution</p>\n<p>This class provides clean lifecycle management with start/stop methods\nand automatic error handling with event store integration.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<p><a href=\"#id88\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id89\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id90\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id91\">`</span></a>python\ncmd_interface = CommandInterface(</p>\n<blockquote>\n<div><p>orchestrator=orchestrator,\nzmq_address=\u201d<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"tcp://\">tcp://</a><a href=\"#id92\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id93\">*</span></a>:5555\u201d,\nallowed_commands={\u201cps\u201d, \u201cshutdown\u201d},\nevent_store=event_store,\nlogger=logger</p>\n</div></blockquote>\n<p>)</p>\n<p># Start command interface\ncmd_interface.start()</p>\n<p># Later, during shutdown\ncmd_interface.stop()\n<a href=\"#id94\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id95\">``</span></a><a href=\"#id96\"><span class=\"problematic\" id=\"id97\">`</span></a></p>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Thread Safety:</dt><dd><p>This class is thread-safe. The ChannelHandler runs in a separate thread\nand handles command messages asynchronously.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>zmq_address</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>allowed_commands</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#set\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>set</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>] </em><em>| </em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>event_store</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.event_store.EventStore\"><em>EventStore</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>logger</strong> (<em>Logger</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.start\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.start\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start the command interface.</p>\n<p>Creates and starts a ChannelHandler thread to process incoming\ncommand messages asynchronously. The handler will continuously\npoll the command channel and invoke handle_command for each message.</p>\n<p>This method should be called during orchestrator initialization.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#RuntimeError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>RuntimeError</strong></a> \u2013 If command interface is already started</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.stop\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">timeout</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">2.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.stop\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop the command interface gracefully.</p>\n<p>Stops the channel handler thread and closes the command channel.\nThis method blocks until the handler thread terminates or timeout expires.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum time to wait for handler thread to stop (seconds)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.handle_command\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">handle_command</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">request_msg</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.handle_command\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Process external command from CLI client.</p>\n<p>This method is invoked by ChannelHandler for each incoming command message.\nIt validates the request, executes the command via CommandHandler, tracks\nerrors to event store, and sends response back to the client.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>request_msg</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a>) \u2013 ServiceMessage containing command request</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Error Handling:</dt><dd><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>Validation errors are tracked to event store and returned as error responses</p></li>\n<li><p>Command execution errors are caught, logged, tracked, and returned as error responses</p></li>\n<li><p>All errors result in structured ServiceMessage error responses sent back to client</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.is_running\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_running</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.command_interface.CommandInterface.is_running\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if command interface is currently running.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if channel handler is running, False otherwise</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-channel-handler\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<p>Channel Handler Module</p>\n<p>This module provides the ChannelHandler class for managing message channel\ncommunication in separate threads, encapsulating thread lifecycle management.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelHandler</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message_handler</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'ChannelHandler'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">logger</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">poll_timeout</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>Handles message channel communication in a separate thread.</p>\n<p>Encapsulates thread lifecycle management for message processing,\nproviding a clean interface for starting, stopping, and handling\nmessages from a MessageChannel.</p>\n<p>This class follows the Single Responsibility Principle by managing\nonly the thread lifecycle and message polling, delegating message\nprocessing to a provided callback function.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>channel</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\"><em>MessageChannel</em></a>) \u2013 The message channel to monitor.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>message_handler</strong> (<em>Callable</em>) \u2013 Callback function to process received messages.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 Thread name for identification and logging.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>logger</strong> \u2013 Logger instance for debugging and error tracking.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>poll_timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Timeout for channel polling in seconds.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>channel</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.MessageChannel\"><em>MessageChannel</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>message_handler</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Callable\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Callable</em></a><em>[</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../utilities/#PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.utilities.messaging.ServiceMessage\"><em>ServiceMessage</em></a><em>]</em><em>, </em><em>None</em><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>poll_timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># Create a handler for agent messages</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">handler</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">ChannelHandler</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">channel</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">msg_channel</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">message_handler</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">orchestrator</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">handle_agent_message</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;AgentMessageHandler&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">logger</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">orchestrator</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logger</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">poll_timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">handler</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"c1\"># ... do work ...</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">handler</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">stop</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">2.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler.start\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler.start\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start the message handling thread.</p>\n<p>Creates and starts a daemon thread that continuously polls the message channel\nand invokes the message handler callback for each received message.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>If the handler is already running, this method logs a warning and returns.</p></li>\n<li><p>The thread is created as a daemon to allow graceful application shutdown.</p></li>\n<li><p>Uses the configured name for easy identification in thread dumps.</p></li>\n</ul>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler.stop\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">timeout</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">2.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler.stop\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop the message handling thread.</p>\n<p>Signals the thread to stop and waits for it to terminate gracefully.\nIf the thread doesn\u2019t stop within the timeout period, a warning is logged.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>timeout</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>float</em></a>) \u2013 Maximum time in seconds to wait for thread termination.\nDefaults to 2.0 seconds.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>This method is idempotent - calling it multiple times is safe.</p></li>\n<li><p>The thread will complete processing the current message before stopping.</p></li>\n<li><p>If the thread is stuck, it will be left as a daemon and eventually\nterminated when the application exits.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler.is_running\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_running</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.channel_handler.ChannelHandler.is_running\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if the handler is currently running.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if the handler thread is active, False otherwise.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory\">\n<span id=\"pyorchestrate-core-orchestrator-memory\"></span><h2>PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">AgentEntry</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_class</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">control_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">state_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">config</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">plugin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record_event_callback</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>AgentEntry is a class that stores metadata and the instance of an agent.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<p>You can access state and control events to manage the agent\u2019s lifecycle.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Examples</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">Orchestrator</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">models</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">FileWriter</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">orchestrator</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">Orchestrator</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;CoolOrchestrator&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">fw_agent</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">AgentEntry</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">orchestrator</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">register_agent</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FileWriter</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;FileWriter&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">orchestrator</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">start</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">fw_agent</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">state_events</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ready_event</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wait</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;agent is now ready&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_class</strong> (<em>Type</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\"><em>BaseAgent</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 The class of the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 The name of the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>BaseAgent.ControlEvents</em></a>) \u2013 Control events for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>BaseAgent.StateEvents</em></a>) \u2013 State events for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>config</strong> (<em>Optional</em><em>[</em><em>BaseConfig</em><em>]</em>) \u2013 Custom configuration for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>plugin</strong> (<em>Optional</em><em>[</em><em>BasePlugin</em><em>]</em>) \u2013 Custom plugin for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_record_event_callback</strong> (<em>Optional</em><em>[</em><em>Any</em><em>]</em>) \u2013 Callback to record events.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>kwargs</strong> (<em>Any</em>) \u2013 Additional keyword arguments for the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>instance</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\"><em>BaseAgent</em></a>) \u2013 The agent instance.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_class</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Type\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Type</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\"><em>AgentProtocol</em></a><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>ControlEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>StateEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><em>BaseClassConfig</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>plugin</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\"><em>BaseClassPlugin</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>record_event_callback</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Any\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Any</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>kwargs</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Any\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Any</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.start\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.start\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.stop\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.stop\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.join\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">join</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.join\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Join the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.restart\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">restart</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.restart\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Restart the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.status\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">status</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.status\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the status of the agent</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.instance\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">instance</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\"><span class=\"pre\">AgentProtocol</span></a></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.instance\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>The agent instance.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\">BaseAgent</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id98\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id98\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id99\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id99\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id100\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">join</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id100\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Join the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id101\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">restart</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id101\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Restart the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.is_alive\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_alive</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.is_alive\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check if the agent instance is alive.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if the agent instance is alive, False otherwise.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">bool</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id102\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">status</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id102\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get agent status.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<p>The status is a string containing the following information:</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>Whether the agent is alive.</p></li>\n<li><p>Whether the agent is a daemon.</p></li>\n<li><p>The agent\u2019s ident (if it is a process).</p></li>\n<li><p>The agent\u2019s PID (if it is a process).</p></li>\n</ul>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Agent status.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.initialize_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">initialize_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry.initialize_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create agent instance.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>If custom agent configuration is not provided, the default</dt><dd><p>configuration will be used (agent_class.Config).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</li>\n<li><dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>If custom agent plugin is not provided, the default plugin will</dt><dd><p>be used (agent_class.Plugin).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>A group of agents.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group.add_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group.add_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Aggiunge un agente (rappresentato dal suo nome) al gruppo.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group.remove_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">remove_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group.remove_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Rimuove un agente dal gruppo.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OMemory</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/functions.html#object\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">object</span></code></a></p>\n<p>OMemory is a class that stores agents and groups of agents.</p>\n<p>Agents are stored as <cite>AgentEntry</cite> objects, which contain some metadata and the agent instance.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>_agents</strong> (<em>Dict</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\"><em>AgentEntry</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 Map from agent name to <cite>AgentEntry</cite> object.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_groups</strong> (<em>Dict</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\"><em>Group</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 Map from group name to <cite>Group</cite> object.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_agent_stats</strong> (<em>Dict</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><em>List</em><em>[</em><em>Dict</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a><em>, </em><em>Any</em><em>]</em><em>]</em><em>]</em>) \u2013 mappa dell\u2019agente con una lista di eventi registrati.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.add_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.add_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add an agent to the orchestrator memory.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_class</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Type\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Type</em></a><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\"><em>AgentProtocol</em></a><em>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_config</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassConfig\"><em>BaseClassConfig</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_plugin</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../base/#PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.base.base.BaseClassPlugin\"><em>BaseClassPlugin</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>ControlEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>StateEvents</em></a><em> | </em><em>None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>kwargs</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.Any\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>Any</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\"><em>AgentEntry</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent_entry\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent_entry</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent_entry\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the <cite>AgentEntry</cite> object corresponding to the provided name.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent_instance\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent_instance</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent_instance\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the agent instance for the provided name.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.create_group\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">create_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.create_group\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create an empty group if it doesn\u2019t already exist.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.add_agent_to_group\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_agent_to_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.add_agent_to_group\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add an existing agent to the specified group.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.remove_agent_from_group\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">remove_agent_from_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.remove_agent_from_group\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Remove an agent from the specified group.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_group\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_group\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the <cite>Group</cite> object if it exists.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\"><em>Group</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_group_agents\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_group_agents</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_group_agents\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the list of agent instances belonging to the group.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\"><em>AgentProtocol</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.start_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">start_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.start_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Start the agent with the given name.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.stop_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">stop_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.stop_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Stop the agent with the given name.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.join_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">join_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.join_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Join the agent with the given name.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.restart_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">restart_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.restart_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Restart the agent with the given name.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.agents\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">agents</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.agents\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the list of all <cite>AgentEntry</cite> objects</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent_stats\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent_stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent_stats\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the event log for the specified agent</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">list</a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#dict\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">dict</a>[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>datetime</em></a>]] | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id103\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">agents</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><span class=\"pre\">list</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\"><span class=\"pre\">AgentEntry</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id103\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return the list of all <cite>AgentEntry</cite> objects.</p>\n<p>These objects contain all the information needed to manage an agent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>List of all agents.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">list</a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id104\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_class</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_config</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">custom_plugin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">control_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">state_events</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">**</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">kwargs</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id104\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Store an agent in the orchestrator memory.</p>\n<p>Data will be stored as an <cite>AgentEntry</cite> object, which contains metadata and the agent instance. The agent will be\ninitialized and its control events will be set to ready by default.</p>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p>\n<p>Every agent has a set of events that can be used to control its lifecycle. By default, all <cite>ControlEvents</cite> are\nset to ready. If no custom events are provided, the default events will be created.</p>\n<p>Events from agents are handled centrally by the orchestrator\u2019s event manager.\nAgents communicate with the orchestrator via message channel.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_class</strong> (<em>Type</em><em>[</em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent\"><em>BaseAgent</em></a><em>]</em>) \u2013 The class of the agent to store.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 The name of the agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_config</strong> (<em>BaseConfig</em><em>, </em><em>optional</em>) \u2013 Custom configuration for the agent. Defaults to None.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>custom_plugin</strong> (<em>BasePlugin</em><em>, </em><em>optional</em>) \u2013 Custom plugin for the agent. Defaults to None.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>control_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.ControlEvents\"><em>BaseAgent.ControlEvents</em></a><em>, </em><em>optional</em>) \u2013 Control events for the agent. Defaults to None.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>state_events</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.BaseAgent.StateEvents\"><em>BaseAgent.StateEvents</em></a><em>, </em><em>optional</em>) \u2013 State events for the agent. Defaults to None.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>kwargs</strong> (<em>Any</em>) \u2013 Additional keyword arguments for the agent.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The <cite>AgentEntry</cite> object corresponding to the stored agent.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a></p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If the agent already exists.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id105\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">create_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">group_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id105\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Crea un gruppo vuoto, se non esiste gi\u00e0.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id106\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_agent_to_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">group_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id106\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Aggiunge un agente esistente al gruppo specificato (se il gruppo esiste).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id107\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">remove_agent_from_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">group_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id107\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Rimuove un agente dal gruppo specificato (se il gruppo esiste).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id108\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_group</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">group_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id108\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Ritorna l\u2019oggetto <cite>Group</cite>, se esiste.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.Group\"><em>Group</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id109\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_group_agents</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">group_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id109\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Ritorna la lista delle istanze degli agenti appartenenti al gruppo.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>group_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/typing.html#typing.List\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>List</em></a>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../agent/#PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.agent.base_agent.AgentProtocol\"><em>AgentProtocol</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id110\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent_stats</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">agent_name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id110\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return the event log for the specified agent.</p>\n<p>If the agent does not exist or has no events, return None.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>agent_name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 The name of the agent.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The event log for the agent or None.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>Optional[List[Dict[<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\">str</a>, datetime]]]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.OMemory.get_agent\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the <cite>AgentEntry</cite> object corresponding to the provided name.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 The name of the agent to retrieve.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The <cite>AgentEntry</cite> object corresponding to the provided name, or None if not found.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\" title=\"PyOrchestrate.core.orchestrator.memory.AgentEntry\">AgentEntry</a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 If the agent is not found.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"id111\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_agent_instance</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#id111\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the agent instance for the provided name.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>name</strong> (<a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.11)\"><em>str</em></a>) \u2013 The name of the agent to retrieve.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The agent instance, or None if not found.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>ProcessAgent | ThreadAgent | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n</section>\n", "metatags": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n", "rellinks": [["genindex